From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:54:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Meta OAuth / scheduled sync: security corrections

- OAuth state is single-use: its nonce is recorded hashed (action_otps, action meta_oauth_state) at start and consumed by
  one atomic UPDATE at the callback; replayed, concurrent, expired, forged, wrong-person and revoked-permission attempts fail
- META_APP_SECRET is required on its own (no fallback to the webhook signing secrets META_APP_SECRETS)
- least privilege: required vs optional (business_management) scopes; ads_read moved to the later Insights phase;
  ads_management kept with Meta's documented reason (a lead's campaign_id / ad_id)
- token answers validated; debug_token must show a valid user token of our app; missing required permissions leave a
  working connection untouched; all Meta calls go through metaFetch (no URL / cause in errors, never logged)
- start rate limit kept in the database; e-mailed code rate limit ignores OAuth nonces
- scheduled run budget 18 s inside the 30 s function limit (5-minute claim cannot lapse mid-run); each Meta lead taken
  under a transaction-scoped advisory lock (no duplicate, no unique-index error under overlap)
- meta-sync.yml fails on missing secret, 401/403, 5xx / timeouts after bounded retries, unexpected statuses, invalid
  answers and syncs with errors

No migration. Nothing applied to production.

